course: dictionary
lesson: 924
title: One word, many meanings: blend
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which meaning to use. Blend is one of these words. Its main meaning is to mix things together so they become one. «Reading is blending: you say the sounds and push them together into the word.» Here blending means joining sounds together.
explain: To blend in is a different meaning: to look or sound like the things around you so nobody notices you. «So its brown-grey feathers blend with the ground» tells you the feathers look like the ground. Ask yourself: is something being mixed, or is something being hidden? That question points you to the right meaning.
explain: Blend can also be a noun, meaning a mixture of different things. «A family made by joining two families is often called a blended family.» Here blended means made from two families mixed together. To check, swap in a word like mixed and see whether the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Small clue words help too. Look for together, in, of and a blend of. If you see «blend in» or «a blend of», the meaning is already almost given to you.
fact: Blend (verb) means to mix two or more things together so they become one.
fact: A blend (noun) is a mixture of different things.
fact: To blend in means to look or sound like the things around you so you are not noticed.
fact: In phonics, a blend is two or three letters said together quickly, like «bl», «st» or «str».
fact: The same word can change its job: blend, blends, blended and blending all come from the same word, and the sentence shows which meaning is in use.
exercise: «Reading is blending: you say the sounds and push them together into the word.» In this sentence, what does blending mean? | Cooking a thick soup | *Joining sounds together so they make one word | Hiding from someone | Painting a picture with soft colours
exercise: «So its brown-grey feathers blend with the ground.» What does blend with the ground suggest? | *Look like the ground, so it is hard to see | Run fast across the ground | Dig a hole in the soil | Lie down and go to sleep
exercise: «A family made by joining two families is often called a blended family.» What does blended mean here? | Painted in many colours | Hidden behind a tree | *Made from two families mixed together | Very fast
test: «Animation is a lovely trick on your brain: lots of still pictures are shown so fast that your eyes and brain blend them into movement.» What does blend mean here? | *Mix them together so they become movement | Hide them away | Count them one by one | Colour them in with crayons
test: Which of these is a phonics blend? | *str | cat | hop | pig
exam: Which sentence uses blend to mean a mixture? | She will blend the banana and milk in the bowl. | *A smoothie is a blend of fruit and juice. | He tried to blend in with the crowd so nobody saw him. | They blend their voices together when they sing.
